  "problem": "There is a proportional relationship between the time $t$ (in seconds) that Jack runs and the distance $d$ (in meters) he covers.\n\n| Time ($t$) | Meters ($d$) |\n| --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $7$ |\n| $3$ | $21$ |\n| $5$ | $35$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Jack runs $35$ meters in $5$ seconds.\n\nII. The unit rate is $6$ meters per second.\n\nIII. If Jack runs for $7$ seconds, he covers $49$ meters.",
